# The pinned cell library is verified BYTE FOR BYTE against lib.lock
# (tools/verify_lib.py, run on every gds build). Git's line-ending conversion
# would rewrite those bytes on checkout — CRLF on Windows, LF on Linux — and the
# sha256 pin would fail on one platform or the other, or worse, pass locally and
# fail only in the submission build. Treat every library artifact as binary so
# what is committed is exactly what is verified and exactly what is hardened.
lib/** -text

# The committed all-own gate netlist is the SUBMITTED source (see info.yaml).
# Same argument: it must not be rewritten by anything.
harden/vslice_gates.v -text
